{"timestamp": "2026-08-10T12:27:31.431745+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-0297f93c-5075-4675-b20d-1bf841fa58ca', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You design one complete lesson.\\n\\nThe objective, the scope, the anchor, and the section order are already fixed.\\nYou do not reopen them. Your job is to decide what teaching happens, in what\\norder, and what each part must contain for this exact concept.\\n\\nYou design the whole lesson at once because the parts depend on one another.\\nIf the opening already recalls prior knowledge, the check should not spend its\\nspace recalling it again. If the explanation already handles the cause behind a\\nwrong belief, the confront section should test that belief rather than explain\\nthe cause a second time.\\n\\nYou choose no formats. You will not see any.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE BUILDING\\n\\n  Resource: Lesson (lesson)\\n\\n  A lesson is the default full teaching resource. It introduces a concept,\\n  builds understanding, models the method, gives students guided-to-independent\\n  practice, and closes with a retention check.\\n  \\n  A lesson teaches before it asks students to perform independently. It is not\\n  a worksheet, not a quick reference, and not a quiz. The teacher should be\\n  able to use it as the main classroom arc for first contact with a concept.\\n  \\n  The pedagogical arc is: orient -> build -> model -> practice -> close.\\n  Every section must serve that arc. The planner must not skip the modelling\\n  step, and it must not turn the close into a second teaching section.\\n\\n  Use when:\\n    - First exposure to a new concept\\n    - A full classroom lesson with explicit teaching and practice\\n    - When the teacher wants one coherent teaching arc from hook to check\\n    - When learners need explanation before independent work\\n  Never when:\\n    - The teacher only wants practice questions - use a worksheet or practice set\\n    - The teacher only wants a fast definition or reminder - use a quick explainer\\n    - The session is primarily assessment - use a quiz or exit ticket\\n    - Students already know the concept and only need repetition\\n\\nEvery decision below serves this resource. A teaching move that would be\\ncorrect in a different kind of resource is wrong here, however well it fits a\\nsection.\\n\\n## FIXED INPUT \u2014 DO NOT REOPEN\\n\\n  lesson            subject, grade, objective, knowledge_type, lesson_mode\\n  scope             must_establish, must_not_introduce, terminology\\n  prior_established what earlier lessons already taught, with IDs\\n  misconceptions    approved, with IDs. Zero to three. Never invent one.\\n  anchor            the concrete case, with ID. Chosen upstream.\\n  slots             ordered, each with a fixed purpose and typical_intents\\n  approved_item_ids assessment items already written and approved, with IDs\\n  assessment_source_policy\\n                    typed item IDs, eligible assessment intents, and the\\n                    exact ownership limits for source_question_ids\\n  limits            max blocks per section, max blocks per lesson\\n\\n## THE VOCABULARY\\n\\n  permitted intents   every intent you may use. Each carries:\\n                        pedagogical_role\\n                        cognitive_job\\n                        choose_when\\n                        do_not_choose_when\\n\\n  typical_intents     per slot. What that slot usually needs.\\n                      A starting point, NOT a fence.\\n\\n  excluded intents    with reasons. A hard wall. Never use one.\\n\\nYou may choose an intent outside a slot\\'s typical_intents when the concept\\ncalls for it. That is a normal, expected decision. It requires a\\ndeparture_reason and nothing more.\\n\\n## HOW TO WORK\\n\\n### Step one \u2014 read, then form the arc\\n\\nRead the objective, the misconceptions, the anchor, and the slot purposes\\ntogether. Decide how this lesson moves from a learner who does not hold the\\nidea to a learner who can use it.\\n\\nWrite that as `arc`: two or three sentences a teacher could read aloud.\\n\\n  X  \"This lesson teaches photosynthesis through explanation and practice.\"\\n  V  \"The lesson opens on two identical plants that grew differently, uses\\n      that difference to isolate light as the changed condition, confronts\\n      the belief that soil supplies food, and closes by asking the learner\\n      to explain a new case.\"\\n\\nThe arc is a commitment. Everything after it must serve it.\\n\\n### Step two \u2014 decide how the anchor is used\\n\\nThe anchor is fixed. You decide what each section does with it.\\n\\nIntroduce it once. Return to it. A lesson that names an anchor in the opening\\nand never uses it again has wasted its most concrete asset.\\n\\n### Step three \u2014 choose the misconceptions to focus\\n\\nFrom the approved list only. Zero is a legitimate answer for a recall-heavy\\nobjective. Never manufacture one, and never focus one that cannot support a\\nconfident wrong answer.\\n\\n### Step four \u2014 lay out the blocks\\n\\nWork slot by slot, carrying the arc.\\n\\nFor each slot:\\n\\n  1. Read the slot purpose against the objective and the anchor.\\n     What must happen HERE, for THIS concept?\\n\\n  2. Read choose_when for the typical intents.\\n     Then read do_not_choose_when.\\n\\n     do_not_choose_when is the important one. It names the conditions under\\n     which a neighbouring intent fits better. If a clause describes this\\n     concept, that intent is out.\\n\\n  3. If none of the typical intents fits, look at the permitted list.\\n     Choosing from it is normal. Write a departure_reason.\\n\\n  4. Decide how many blocks. One is common. Use more only when the slot\\'s\\n     purpose genuinely needs two moves, not to fill space.\\n\\n  5. Write the brief.\\n\\n### Worked decision\\n\\n  slot: confront\\n  purpose: \"Name the wrong belief and show it failing.\"\\n  typical_intents: [diagnose-misconception, warn, compare]\\n  objective: \"explain why plants cannot make food in darkness\"\\n  misconception-1: \"plants take food from the soil\"\\n\\n    diagnose-misconception\\n      choose_when: a named, real misconception exists and a wrong answer can\\n                   be written that only a learner holding it would confidently\\n                   choose\\n      -> misconception-1 is on the card and is exactly this. Matches.\\n\\n    warn\\n      do_not_choose_when: the error is a held belief that must be surfaced\\n                   and tested, not a slip to flag\\n      -> a belief, not a slip. Out.\\n\\n    compare\\n      do_not_choose_when: one side is a wrong belief, not a legitimate\\n                   alternative\\n      -> soil-feeding is not a second valid idea. Out.\\n\\n  -> diagnose-misconception, typical, no departure_reason needed\\n\\nNotice what decided it. Not the slot name and not the intent label. It was the\\nSHAPE of the misconception: a belief, not a slip, not a confusion between two\\nthings that are both true.\\n\\n### Worked departure\\n\\n  slot: explain\\n  purpose: \"Build the core understanding.\"\\n  typical_intents: [explain, explain-cause]\\n  objective: \"explain why plants cannot make food in darkness\"\\n\\n  Both typical intents are plausible. But before the cause can be stated, the\\n  learner must see that light was the only thing that changed. That is a\\n  controlled contrast, not an explanation.\\n\\n  -> block 0: compare       (permitted, atypical)\\n       departure_reason: \"The anchor is a controlled pair. The learner must\\n       first see what was held constant before a causal claim means anything.\\n       Explaining the cause first would leave the contrast unexamined.\"\\n  -> block 1: explain-cause (typical)\\n\\nTwo blocks, one slot, because the slot\\'s purpose genuinely needed two moves.\\n\\n## THE BRIEF\\n\\nThe brief is what the writer works from. Anything you leave out will not\\nappear on the page.\\n\\nA brief must answer:\\n\\n  What exact content belongs here?\\n  Which concept, case, or term does it use?\\n  What should change in the learner\\'s understanding?\\n  What must it NOT do?\\n\\n  X  \"Explain the cause clearly.\"\\n  X  \"Give a useful example.\"\\n  X  \"Introduce the topic in an engaging way.\"\\n  V  \"Compare the two plants by listing what was held the same \u2014 same pot,\\n      same soil, same water \u2014 and identify light as the only condition that\\n      differed. Do not yet say what light does.\"\\n\\nRules:\\n\\n  - Name concrete things. The anchor by name, the actual terms, the real\\n    numbers. A brief that says \"an example\" produces a generic example.\\n  - Use terminology from scope.terminology. Never use a term from\\n    must_not_introduce.\\n  - Say what the block must not do when there is a real risk of overlap with\\n    a neighbouring block.\\n  - If your brief would fit another lesson unchanged, it is too vague.\\n  - Never name a format. No prose, table, list, figure, worked example,\\n    questions, aside, choices. Describe what must be said, not what shape\\n    says it.\\n\\n**The last brief matters as much as the first.** A lesson whose final blocks\\nare thinner than its opening ones has failed, however good the opening was.\\nBefore you finish, re-read your last brief against your first.\\n\\n## EVIDENCE\\n\\nEvery block carries two evidence fields. Both are required.\\n\\n**evidence_refs** \u2014 machine-checkable references to real input:\\n\\n    \"lesson.objective\"\\n    \"scope.must_establish[0]\"\\n    \"misconception-1\"\\n    \"anchor.anchor-plant-window\"\\n    \"prior-1\"\\n    \"slot.explain.purpose\"\\n\\nOnly reference IDs that exist in the input. Every ref is validated.\\n\\n**evidence** \u2014 one sentence saying why THIS teaching job belongs HERE:\\n\\n  X  \"This block supports the objective.\"\\n  X  \"This seemed pedagogically appropriate.\"\\n  X  \"The slot needs an explanation.\"\\n  V  \"The objective asks WHY food is not made in darkness. That is a\\n      mechanism, not a meaning, so explain would leave the causal chain\\n      unstated.\"\\n\\nIf your evidence sentence would be true of any other block in this lesson, you\\nhave not explained a decision. Write it again.\\n\\n## APPROVED ASSESSMENT SOURCES\\n\\nYou may attach an already-approved item to a teaching block only under the\\nrules in `assessment_source_policy`.\\n\\nFor the current multiple-choice items, `source_question_ids` is either empty\\nor a singleton array containing exactly one approved item ID. Select the one\\nitem that best checks the lesson objective. You do not need to use every\\napproved item, and you must not collect several items into one block.\\n\\nA non-empty `source_question_ids` is legal only when the block\\'s intent is in\\n`assessment_source_policy.eligible_intents`. Leave it empty on every other\\nblock. Each approved item may be owned by at most one block.\\n\\nYou may NOT write question text, stems, options, or answers. Those already\\nexist and were approved separately. You also do not choose whether an item is\\nrendered as open response or multiple choice; its typed source record decides\\nthat later.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n  Never change the objective, scope, anchor identity, slot set, or slot order.\\n  Never use an excluded intent.\\n  Never invent a misconception, or focus one not on the approved list.\\n  Never name a page object, format, or layout anywhere in your output.\\n  Never emit a heading block. Headings come from section titles.\\n  Never write question content.\\n  Never put multiple approved item IDs in one multiple-choice source array.\\n  Never attach an approved item to a non-assessment intent.\\n  Never exceed the block limits.\\n  Never introduce a term from must_not_introduce.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only. No preamble, no code fences, no commentary.\\n\\n{\\n  \"arc\": str,\\n  \"anchor_usage\": { \"<slot_id>\": str, ... },\\n  \"misconception_focus_ids\": [str],\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"slot_id\": str,\\n      \"specific_purpose\": str,\\n      \"transition\": str | null,\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": str,\\n          \"position\": int,\\n          \"intent\": str,\\n          \"brief\": str,\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [str],\\n          \"evidence\": str,\\n          \"departure_reason\": str | null,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": [str]\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\nBlock IDs follow `{slot_id}-b{n}`, starting at 1. Positions are 0-based and\\ncontiguous within each section. Sections appear in skeleton order.\\n\\n`transition` is null for the first section. For every other section, say in\\none sentence what the previous section left the learner ready for.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n  1. Does my arc describe THIS lesson, or any lesson on this topic?\\n  2. Is my last brief as concrete as my first? Re-read both.\\n  3. Did I read do_not_choose_when, or recognise a label?\\n  4. Does every evidence sentence explain a choice, or restate the slot?\\n  5. Is the anchor introduced once and returned to?\\n  6. Does any brief name a format? Remove it.\\n  7. Would any two blocks teach the same thing?\\n  8. Does CHECK actually check the objective, or something adjacent?\\n  9. Is every focused misconception confronted somewhere?\\n 10. Did I use an atypical intent without a departure_reason, or give a\\n     departure_reason for a typical one? Both are errors.\\n 11. Is every non-empty source_question_ids a singleton on an eligible\\n     assessment intent, with no item reused by another block?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"AnchorUsage\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"orient\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"explain\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"confront\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"check\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"AnchorUsage\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"TeachingPlanBlock\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"position\": {\"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"integer\"}, \"intent\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"brief\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence_refs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"evidence\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"departure_reason\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"source_question_ids\": {\"description\": \"Approved assessment-item ownership. Leave empty for a non-assessment block. A multiple-choice source must be the only ID in this array.\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"position\", \"intent\", \"brief\", \"evidence\"], \"title\": \"TeachingPlanBlock\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"TeachingPlanSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"slot_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"specific_purpose\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"transition\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"blocks\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/TeachingPlanBlock\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"slot_id\"], \"title\": \"TeachingPlanSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"arc\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"anchor_usage\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AnchorUsage\"}, \"misconception_focus_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/TeachingPlanSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"arc\", \"anchor_usage\"], \"title\": \"TeachingPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"assessment_source_policy\": {\\n    \"allowed_evidence_refs\": [\\n      \"M1\",\\n      \"M2\",\\n      \"M3\",\\n      \"anchor.anchor-1\",\\n      \"item.c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i1\",\\n      \"item.c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i2\",\\n      \"item.c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i3\",\\n      \"item.c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i4\",\\n      \"item.c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i5\",\\n      \"lesson.objective\",\\n      \"must-1\",\\n      \"must-2\",\\n      \"prior-1\",\\n      \"prior-2\",\\n      \"scope.must_establish.must-1\",\\n      \"scope.must_establish.must-2\",\\n      \"scope.must_establish[0]\",\\n      \"scope.must_establish[1]\",\\n      \"slot.check.purpose\",\\n      \"slot.contrast.purpose\",\\n      \"slot.explain.purpose\",\\n      \"slot.orient.purpose\"\\n    ],\\n    \"approved_sources\": [\\n      {\\n        \"approved_item_id\": \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i1\",\\n        \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"approved_item_id\": \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i2\",\\n        \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"approved_item_id\": \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i3\",\\n        \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"approved_item_id\": \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i4\",\\n        \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"approved_item_id\": \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i5\",\\n        \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"eligible_intents\": [\\n      \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n      \"apply\",\\n      \"check-understanding\",\\n      \"classify\",\\n      \"compare\",\\n      \"connect-back\",\\n      \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n      \"explain-cause\",\\n      \"interpret\",\\n      \"orient\",\\n      \"practise-guided\",\\n      \"practise-independent\",\\n      \"sequence\"\\n    ],\\n    \"forbidden_terminology\": [\\n      \"checks and balances between arms\",\\n      \"how members of each arm are chosen or appointed\",\\n      \"the concept of judicial review or constitutional review\",\\n      \"detailed historical origins of separation of powers\"\\n    ],\\n    \"rules\": {\\n      \"item_kind_is_fixed_upstream\": true,\\n      \"multiple_choice_ids_per_block\": \"0_or_1\",\\n      \"reuse_across_blocks\": \"forbidden\",\\n      \"selection_is_optional\": true,\\n      \"source_only_on_eligible_intent\": true\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \"fixed_input\": {\\n    \"anchor\": {\\n      \"description\": \"Think about a country where one person makes the rules, enforces them, and decides who broke them\\\\u2014t\\\\u2026\",\\n      \"id\": \"anchor-1\"\\n    },\\n    \"approved_item_ids\": [\\n      \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i1\",\\n      \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i2\",\\n      \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i3\",\\n      \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i4\",\\n      \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21:9ec293ca-70a1-4fcf-98f3-f223aa74838a.i5\"\\n    ],\\n    \"lesson\": {\\n      \"grade_level\": \"Grade 6\",\\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"conceptual\",\\n      \"lesson_mode\": \"first_exposure\",\\n      \"objective\": \"identify the three arms of government (executive, legislature, judiciary) and describe what each one does\",\\n      \"path_lesson_id\": \"c4d7b3d7-0031-48b7-8580-8b5672873c21\",\\n      \"subject\": \"History\"\\n    },\\n    \"limits\": {\\n      \"max_blocks_per_section\": 3,\\n      \"max_sections\": 4,\\n      \"max_total_blocks\": 10\\n    },\\n    \"misconceptions\": [\\n      {\\n        \"id\": \"M1\",\\n        \"statement\": \"{\\'id\\': \\'M1\\', \\'description\\': \\'The president makes the laws\\', \\'source\\': \\'drafted\\'}\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"id\": \"M2\",\\n        \"statement\": \"{\\'id\\': \\'M2\\', \\'description\\': \\'The courts enforce the laws\\', \\'source\\': \\'drafted\\'}\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"id\": \"M3\",\\n        \"statement\": \"{\\'id\\': \\'M3\\', \\'description\\': \\'The legislature decides who is guilty\\', \\'source\\': \\'drafted\\'}\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"prior_established\": [\\n      {\\n        \"id\": \"prior-1\",\\n        \"statement\": \"a country is run by a government\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"id\": \"prior-2\",\\n        \"statement\": \"government makes and enforces laws\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"scope\": {\\n      \"must_establish\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"must-1\",\\n          \"statement\": \"the three arms of government: executive, legislature, judiciary\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"must-2\",\\n          \"statement\": \"the role of each arm: the legislature makes laws, the executive enforces laws, the judiciary interprets laws and resolves disputes\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"exclude-1\",\\n          \"statement\": \"checks and balances between arms\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"exclude-2\",\\n          \"statement\": \"how members of each arm are chosen or appointed\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"exclude-3\",\\n          \"statement\": \"the concept of judicial review or constitutional review\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"exclude-4\",\\n          \"statement\": \"detailed historical origins of separation of powers\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"terminology\": [\\n        \"executive\",\\n        \"legislature\",\\n        \"judiciary\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"slots\": [\\n      {\\n        \"max_blocks\": 2,\\n        \"min_blocks\": 1,\\n        \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n        \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"emphasise\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"max_blocks\": 3,\\n        \"min_blocks\": 1,\\n        \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n        \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"name-parts\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"max_blocks\": 3,\\n        \"min_blocks\": 1,\\n        \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n        \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"show-structure\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"max_blocks\": 1,\\n        \"min_blocks\": 1,\\n        \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n        \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\"\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"legality_catalogue_hash\": \"c0250ed98d2f5abca69c19e4cc866ed36f855b8b33ad2c4fdd12ed3ba64db415\",\\n  \"slot_intent_policy\": {\\n    \"check\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"orient\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"trace-flow\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"practise-independent\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"contrast\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"orient\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"trace-flow\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"explain\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"orient\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"trace-flow\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"orient\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"trace-flow\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"orient\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \"teaching_guidance\": {\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"intents\": [\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Prompt recall of concepts required for this lesson. Keep it brief and diagnostic.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Surface prerequisite knowledge\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Require selection and use of the learned idea in a recognizable context.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"apply\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Use knowledge in a familiar situation\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The teacher needs to know right now whether the objective landed, and correct-versus-incorrect is the signal being read.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'wrong answers must identify WHICH wrong model the learner holds\\', \\'practise-independent\\': \\'the purpose is rehearsal rather than measurement\\', \\'reflect\\': \\'there is no correct answer\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Detect immediate misunderstanding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Provide or elicit a rule for category membership and contrast borderline cases.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"classify\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Organize examples into categories\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Two or more named things must be told apart, and the same criteria apply to each.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"compare\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'classify\\': \\'instances are being sorted by a rule rather than two things contrasted\\', \\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'one side is a wrong belief, not a legitimate alternative\\', \\'evaluate\\': \\'one option must be judged better, not merely distinguished\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Expose similarities and differences\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Show which prior idea is being reused and exactly how it supports the current task.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"connect-back\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Make prerequisite dependence explicit\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State what the current idea enables next and the unresolved question that follows.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Bridge current learning to the next idea\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Give a precise learner-appropriate definition, distinguish it from nearby terms, and include notation only when useful.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"define\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Establish precise meaning\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner has not yet seen the method carried out end to end on a real instance, and the method is unambiguous once seen. If the learner has already seen it worked through in this lesson, this condition is no longer met.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'model-thinking\\': \\'the difficulty is choosing between approaches, not executing one\\', \\'derive\\': \\'the result must be justified from prior statements, not computed\\', \\'practise-guided\\': \\'the learner is attempting the work, not watching it\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Model a complete method\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The result must be shown to FOLLOW from statements the learner already accepts, and each transformation needs a stated justification.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"derive\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'demonstrate\\': \\'the point is the procedure, not its justification\\', \\'model-thinking\\': \\'steps are chosen from alternatives rather than compelled\\', \\'explain-cause\\': \\'the chain is physical rather than logical\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Build a result from prior statements\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"A named, real misconception exists on the card, and a wrong answer can be written that only a learner holding it would confidently choose. One block per misconception the card declares \\\\u2014 a misconception not on the card does not exist.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'check-understanding\\': \\'no specific wrong model is known; the check only detects failure\\', \\'warn\\': \\'the error is a slip or lapse, not a held belief\\', \\'compare\\': \\'both sides are legitimate\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Distinguish a known wrong model from the target model\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Set apart only the single statement learners should retain. Do not create multiple competing key ideas.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"emphasise\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Mark a high-value statement\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Require criteria, evidence, a judgment, and limitations.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"evaluate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Judge a claim, method, or evidence\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner must reason about instances they have not seen, and the difficulty is the idea itself \\\\u2014 not its cause, its flow, its arrangement, or a representation of it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"explain\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'explain-cause\\': \\'the objective asks WHY, and a mechanism links cause to result\\', \\'trace-flow\\': \\'something is followed as it moves or changes through a system\\', \\'show-structure\\': \\'the difficulty is arrangement, containment, or hierarchy\\', \\'interpret\\': \\'a specific representation is on the page and must be read\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Build a coherent mental model\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The objective asks why, or what happens if, and there is a mechanism between cause and result that the learner must be able to state.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'explain\\': \\'there is no cause-and-effect chain, only meaning or structure\\', \\'trace-flow\\': \\'the emphasis is on what moves, not on what causes\\', \\'sequence\\': \\'order matters but no causal mechanism does\\', \\'derive\\': \\'the chain is logical rather than physical\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Connect causes, mechanisms, and outcomes\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Explain what a graph, formula, diagram, table, or result means in context.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"interpret\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Translate representation into meaning\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Specify question, variables, observations, and evidence expectations. Avoid pretending a screen simulation is a paper practical.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"investigate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Structure an inquiry or practical\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Provide a short, accurate cue that does not replace understanding.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Support recall with a compact cue\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State why each decision is made, what alternatives were rejected, and what signal triggered the next step.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"model-thinking\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Expose expert decision making\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Identify the important parts of a system or idea and state each part\\'s role.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"name-parts\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Identify constituent elements\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Begin with a concrete phenomenon, dilemma, observation, or question. Do not explain the full idea yet.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"orient\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Open attention and establish a reason to learn\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner can begin the task but will stall without prompts, partial steps, or hints.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'practise-independent\\': \\'support would now be a crutch\\', \\'demonstrate\\': \\'the learner is watching rather than attempting\\', \\'apply\\': \\'the point is first unaided use, not scaffolded rehearsal\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Rehearse with structured support\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner has already succeeded with support and must now perform unaided, with enough repetition for fluency.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'practise-guided\\': \\'the learner has not yet succeeded with support\\', \\'check-understanding\\': \\'the purpose is measurement, not rehearsal\\', \\'transfer\\': \\'the context is deliberately changed\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Rehearse without scaffolding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Ask learners to explain what changed in their thinking, what remains difficult, or which strategy helped.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"reflect\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Prompt learners to examine their understanding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Express steps or events in a meaningful order. Include dependencies and stopping conditions where relevant.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"sequence\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Represent an ordered process\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Show levels, containment, arrangement, or relationships that are hard to infer from prose.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"show-structure\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Reveal spatial or hierarchical organization\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State what the learner should be able to explain, do, compare, or justify.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"state-goal\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Clarify the expected learning outcome\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Restate the minimum complete model, not a list of disconnected facts.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"summarise\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Compress the lesson into essential relationships\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Something identifiable \\\\u2014 matter, energy, information, money, data \\\\u2014 enters, changes, moves, and leaves, and the learner must not lose track of it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"trace-flow\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'sequence\\': \\'the steps are actions taken, not a substance being followed\\', \\'explain-cause\\': \\'the point is why it happens, not where it goes\\', \\'show-structure\\': \\'the arrangement is static and nothing travels through it\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Follow matter, energy, information, or value\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Change surface features enough that learners must recognize the underlying structure.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"transfer\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Use knowledge in a changed context\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"A specific error is predictable at this exact point, and naming it before it happens prevents it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"warn\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'the error is a held belief that must be surfaced and tested, not a slip to flag\\', \\'emphasise\\': \\'the content is a positive statement to retain, not an error to avoid\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Prevent a predictable error\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"projection_hash\": \"a9530874d702efc409dcd4c87658fe037981b8a8a6ed76e1d95a551ff8885870\"\\n  }\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-pro', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'reasoning_effort': 'high', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
